      "problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${c}_{21}=-5\\ne 0.$",
